## Residual risks (return)
| ID | Sev | Residual | Why not 6.1 FAIL |
|----|-----|----------|------------------|
| R1 | MED | `oodac check` type/cap-first: no dual-path `ERR secret` for `env_set`/`setenv` | rc≠0 still fail-closed; emit-c/llvm carry the secret contract for key/value |
| R2 | MED | LLVM (+ check scan) `want=1` skips a0; `emit-llvm` ALLOW `@env_set/@setenv(%OoStr secret, …)` | emit-c full scan BLOCK; IR ABI ≠ libc; no `oo_env_set`; `env_set` a0 also cap-denied |
| R3 | MED | `putenv` / `clearenv` / `environ` **not** SECRETSINK; emit ALLOW `putenv(SECRET)` | not the 6.1 named pair; gcc type-fail; add to sink list later |
| R4 | LOW | stmt public `setenv`/`env_set` emit raw C (let-bind hits unknown-call) | public values only; C type / link fail-closed |
| R5 | MED | User wrapper `wrap` → `env_set(c,k,v)` emit ALLOW (e26) | SPRINT **2.10** `__sec_sink__`; interproc beyond `__fr_secret__` is SECRET_TAINT residual |
| R6 | LOW | `getenv(SECRET)` emit ALLOW; `getenv` sealed but not a secret write sink | read path; `env_get` is the product read sink and **does** refuse |
| R7 | — | No product `oo_env_set` | `CAPS_MATRIX` fail-closed residual; do not claim env write In |
| R8 | LOW | `setenv` not in `is_sealed_env` (only `env_set`/`getenv`/`env_get`) | check cannot cap-deny libc-style `setenv`; type residual |
| R9 | — | Fixture `secret_setenv_pass` / smoke `expect_ok` stale vs unknown-call | harness honesty |
| R10 | — | Full IFC / `#[Secret]` / `${}` / field lattice | SECRET_TAINT; **not** 6.1 |
| R11 | — | 7.1 / 7.2 / 7.10 | **do not reopen**; walker is a 6.1 rail only |

**Explicitly not residuals of this close:** T1 return/alias (e13/e14/e20
BLOCK); T2 string/comment FP (e16/e17 ALLOW); T3 child `PATH` setenv
after `clearenv`.

